06L0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2dcb778ede4329b6e71133d05e099b677ddfe9365950cb12abe1674abb2ad6ed", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:75fcdc0cea9bb4a9e2ed6e49f3df3052b59b2706ed03525efb9a52d6ec57ba9c", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nAccording to the next lemma, a smooth morphism from a predeformation functor to\na predeformation category <MATH_0001> gives rise to a presentation of\n<MATH_0002> by a smooth groupoid in functors.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:156fddf13d3de5d9d9a1295d5d19cadb20a237eeb71e8bd37aaec4a68d4a2ca8", "unit_id": "inventory:formal-defos:06L0:paragraph/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:formal-defos:inventory:formal-defos:06L1:lemma/0001", "hash": "sha256:169526a7143adc5c77e2c8974c270d176ab9a97501f03e510bed190b2c86a5cc", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 252803, "byte_start": 252072, "file": "formal-defos.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:6535c57b638bf467837e1e88e5e7bb5c9e793956028cdda5f5c2a2ee570585a5", "line_end": 6701, "line_start": 6685}, "owner_tag": "06L1", "parent_tag": "06L0", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06L0", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{lemma-smooth-groupoid-in-functors-construction}", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$U : \\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0004": "$f : U \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0007": "$f : U \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0009": "$f : U(k) \\to \\mathcal{F}(k)$", "MATH_0010": "$[f] : [U/R] \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-presentation-construction}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-presentation-morphism}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{lemma}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{lemma}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9c1bac96719bd88222126945b0c78f00597d47ac7cf517a183a1090a8aa8874e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:07d6a3d5950d8338d54f82a2b53df3a2da93acd12da08efee7bae4c19367dedc", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a category cofibered in groupoids over\n<MATH_0002>. Let <MATH_0003>\nbe a functor. Let <MATH_0004> be a smooth morphism of\ncategories cofibered in groupoids. Then:\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0005> is the groupoid in functors on\n<MATH_0006> constructed from <MATH_0007> in\nLemma <REF_0001>, then <MATH_0008>\nis smooth.\n<STRUCT_0004> If <MATH_0009> is essentially surjective,\nthen the morphism <MATH_0010> of\nLemma <REF_0002>\nis an equivalence.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n<STRUCT_0006>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ed7babcb019984b8fc05ad0199225fc5965fa4a782fb62d126de29ebfeedace5", "unit_id": "inventory:formal-defos:06L1:lemma/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:formal-defos:inventory:formal-defos:06L1:proof/0001", "hash": "sha256:0572970d2dddf09ef4b4803b4e38bed9ced6ee04ef1799a5a514f0a41c2872ba", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 253465, "byte_start": 252805, "file": "formal-defos.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:c7cb5253e534e10f491e2297778269d3defa88c141b437e782210d4015004171", "line_end": 6723, "line_start": 6703}, "owner_tag": "06L1", "parent_tag": "06L0", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06L0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nR = U \\times_{f, \\mathcal{F}, f} U \\ar[r]_-s \\ar[d]_t & U\n\\ar[d]^f \\\\\nU \\ar[r]^f & \\mathcal{F}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$t, s$", "MATH_0003": "$t, s$", "MATH_0004": "$f : U \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$[f] : [U/R] \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-presentation-construction}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-smooth-properties}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-smooth-morphism-essentially-surjective}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-presentation-morphism}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2a3396c914cba0753417597517b12fa085f4e2335314185ce8a7642347fc5742", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f437670b8e19e0fb887562174f1108fa4b105e1f91bd34679985615b534a6dba", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nFrom the construction of\nLemma <REF_0001>\nwe have a commutative diagram\n<MATH_0001>\nwhere <MATH_0002> are the first and second projections.  So <MATH_0003> are smooth by\nLemma <REF_0002>.  Hence (1) holds.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nIf the assumption of (2) holds, then by\nLemma <REF_0003>\nthe morphism <MATH_0004> is essentially surjective. Hence by\nLemma <REF_0004>\nthe morphism <MATH_0005> is an equivalence.\n<STRUCT_0004>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:95bee89fdcbc84615169f50b43c3fa5fb932111f9685bc9a94272c37aa77642d", "unit_id": "inventory:formal-defos:06L1:proof/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:formal-defos:inventory:formal-defos:06L6:lemma/0001", "hash": "sha256:cbce8924806ddd63a0c98ca12c19e533581764bccf8e97a732ef63a1ceadbfdc", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 253958, "byte_start": 253467, "file": "formal-defos.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:0f55c19ca1538a297dc537186259766170c27a72